 "ref": "The S-E-C alleged one more detail. Around September twenty seventeen, it said, Horwitz falsely told an investor group he was personally investing in several notes alongside them. According to the S-E-C, the money he put in had been taken from other investors. When those notes paid out in March twenty eighteen, the S-E-C alleged, the group paid him about two point three three million dollars as his share. The S-E-C alleged he combined that money with other investor funds to buy his home, for about five point seven million dollars in cash. When a promoter says he is investing right alongside you, treat it as a claim to check, not as proof.",
